## Autonomy

- Execute the approved plan step by step. Never ask for a go-ahead or whether to continue, commit, run tests, retry or start the next step: decide from the plan, ADRs, repo rules or existing code.
- Stop only with `ESCALATION: <type>` (unplanned architecture; scope/cost/reversibility decision; plan/rules/code contradiction; forbidden action; missing access). One batched message with options, recommendation, consequence, cost.
- In Cursor direct execution a normal session may commit on the current checkout within approved ticket scope with the `Ref:` trailer (see `.cursor/rules/igx-cursor-direct-execution.mdc`). Subagents and delegated modes still follow `may_commit` in `governance/agent-control-plane/role_registry.yaml`. `git push origin development` after quality gates from a clean `development` checkout (fast-forward only; server rejection is a real blocker — no force push). In ChatGPT Direct mode, candidate push and draft PR are permitted only through the authorized Cursor candidate publisher. External acceptance, merge, branch integration and GitHub settings stay human.
- Sub-agents end with `DONE: <line>` or `BLOCKED: <type>: <what, options, recommendation>`; the parent decides alone when plan, ADR, rules or code answer it (`/igx-autonomy`).
- Plan finished: print `PLAN COMPLETE` and a short summary when the approved work is complete (Cursor direct execution per `.cursor/rules/igx-cursor-direct-execution.mdc`).
<!-- igx:authority end -->

## Cursor orchestration

- Cursor parent may be Grok. Workers: Task `model` `composer-2.5` or `composer-2.5-fast` (do not omit `model`). Any other worker model needs an Operator override in that chat. IIAC and G6 are unchanged.

